# Keep the build context small and reproducible.
#
# Everything listed here is either regenerated during the build or must never
# reach the image. The most important line is `.env`: without it, a local
# environment file would be copied into the build context and could end up in an
# image layer — where it stays forever, readable by anyone who pulls the image,
# even if a later layer deletes it.

# Build output — regenerated by the build stage. Copying a local target/ would
# also risk shipping a stale jar built on a different JDK.
target/

# Secrets. Never.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# IDE and OS noise
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# The Maven wrapper is not needed inside the image: the build stage uses the
# Maven bundled in the maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-21 base image.
.mvn/
mvnw
mvnw.cmd
